From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 16:32:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: apple: avd: send the v5 HEVC header on T8132

On the J604 (T8132, avd-fw 0.1 v5-t1) an HEVC Main clip decoded through
VA-API returned no frame, while H.264 and VP9 decoded bit-exact on the
same boot (kernel 7.2.11-15-1.611, hardware-decode check: hevc frames=0).

T8132 is the decoder that T6040 carries. Commit 8b9ba6a2d50c ("media:
apple: avd: send the v5 HEVC header on T6040") found that T6040's first
HEVC job stalled the VP with the pre-v5 header, because T6040 runs the
same v5 firmware generation (avd-fw-v5-t1, hardware revision 4) with the
same VP layout as T8140. Commit 829bcab267ce ("media: apple: avd:
advertise T6040 HEVC with h265-capable firmware") then records that
T6040 decodes HEVC with the v5 header. The T8132 variant has the same
firmware image, revision and VP layout, and was the one variant of that
generation still sending the pre-v5 header. Send it the v5 header too.

AVD_QUIRK_HEVC_V5_HEADER only changes the HEVC program (the DMA
configuration words and the reserved scratch slot); H.264, VP9 and AV1
submissions and their pacing are unchanged (the T8140 pacing lives in
AVD_QUIRK_V5_QUEUE_PACING, which T8132 does not take).

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-drv.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-drv.c b/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-drv.c
index b6e071493a..08cf08ce69 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-drv.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-drv.c
@@ -470,6 +470,12 @@ static const struct avd_variant avd_t8140_variant = {
 	.quirks = AVD_QUIRK_HEVC_V5_HEADER | AVD_QUIRK_V5_QUEUE_PACING,
 };
 
+/*
+ * T8132 (M4): the decoder T6040 also carries, on the same v5 firmware
+ * generation (avd-fw-v5-t1, hardware revision 4) and VP layout, so its HEVC
+ * jobs take the v5 header as T6040's and T8140's do. With the pre-v5 header
+ * the first HEVC job returned no frame.
+ */
 static const struct avd_variant avd_t8132_variant = {
 	.vp_slots = {
 		[AVD_CODEC_HEVC] = 4,
@@ -489,6 +495,7 @@ static const struct avd_variant avd_t8132_variant = {
 	.submit_offset = 0x40,
 	.submit_queue_max_offset = 0x44,
 	.submit_queue_status_offset = 0x7c,
+	.quirks = AVD_QUIRK_HEVC_V5_HEADER,
 };
 
 /*
